			"date": "2023-10-25T13:24:47.162Z",
			"content": "<p>I think a mixture of all 3 of those things is likely true.</p><p>I am very worried about demographics and over-indexing on popularity as a method for prioritization.</p><p>If the average responder to a State of ___ survey is Man Who Thinks React Is Good, Actually—will the outcomes of those survey results (if used for prioritization decisions) improve the web platform or diminish it?</p><p>What values do we want the web to have and how can we use those to inform prioritization instead of popularity?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
